          "question": "The unit vector $\\hat{n}$ perpendicular to both $\\vec{a}=\\hat{i}+\\hat{j}$ and $\\vec{b}=\\hat{j}+\\hat{k}$, such that $\\vec{a}$, $\\vec{b}$, $\\hat{n}$ form a right-handed system, is:",
          "options": [
            "$\\dfrac{-\\hat{i}+\\hat{j}-\\hat{k}}{\\sqrt{3}}$",
            "$\\dfrac{\\hat{i}+\\hat{j}+\\hat{k}}{\\sqrt{3}}$",
            "$\\hat{i}-\\hat{j}+\\hat{k}$",
            "$\\dfrac{\\hat{i}-\\hat{j}+\\hat{k}}{\\sqrt{3}}$"
          ],
          "solution": {
            "answer": "(D) $\\dfrac{\\hat{i}-\\hat{j}+\\hat{k}}{\\sqrt{3}}$",
            "concept": "$\\vec{a}$, $\\vec{b}$, $\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b}$ form a right-handed system, so $\\hat{n}=\\dfrac{\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b}}{|\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b}|}$.",
            "steps": [
              {
                "do": "For a right-handed system, $\\hat{n}$ is along $\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b}$ (in this order).",
                "math": "\\hat{n} = \\dfrac{\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b}}{|\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b}|}"
              },
              {
                "do": "Find the cross product.",
                "math": "\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\hat{i} & \\hat{j} & \\hat{k} \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\end{vmatrix} = \\hat{i}-\\hat{j}+\\hat{k}"
              },
              {
                "do": "Divide by its magnitude $\\sqrt{1+1+1}=\\sqrt{3}$.",
                "math": "\\hat{n} = \\dfrac{\\hat{i}-\\hat{j}+\\hat{k}}{\\sqrt{3}}",
                "marks": 1
              },
              {
                "do": "Hence the answer is option (D)."
              }
            ],
            "mistake": "Choosing (A): that is along $\\vec{b}\\times\\vec{a}$, the left-handed order; (C) is not a unit vector."
